; regression test: found while assessing natural.kurt's (never-before-exercised) induction
; axiom for the first time -- a *failed* derivation of a conditioned quantifier goal
; (`forall $x in Nat ...`, `forall $x>0 ...`, and similarly for `exists`) used to crash with an
; internal `AssertionError` instead of raising a clean `ProofError`. Root cause:
; `remove_outer_forall_quantifiers` desugars `forall $x (cond) body` into
; `forall $x (cond implies body)` by synthesizing a plain `Token(label='SYMBOL',
; value='implies')` with no `column` set (defaults to `None`); that's harmless when
; derivation *succeeds*, since the synthetic token never gets shown to the user -- but when
; derivation *fails*, `get_column` (building the ProofError's message) asserts every token it
; walks down to has a real integer column, and crashes here instead. This has nothing to do
; with `natural.kurt`/induction specifically -- any conditioned-quantifier goal that fails to
; derive hits it (confirmed independently with `set.kurt`'s `in`, no `natural.kurt` involved).
; Fixed by giving the synthetic `implies` token a column borrowed from the condition it wraps.
; (Since then, a condition isn't turned into an implication by the engine at all -- see
; doc/kurt-soundness.md §8.11 -- so there is no synthetic token any more.)
load set, logic
bool P
arity P 1
const P, Nat
expect "ProofError"
    forall $x in Nat  P $x

